  "notes": [
    "Arms differ in one thing only. WITH: the workspace CLAUDE.md documents the dt CLI. MCP: the generic workspace text plus the repository's stdio design-system MCP server attached. MCP + POINTER: the MCP arm plus one line in the workspace naming the server. WITHOUT: the generic workspace text. Every arm has identical repository access, task, model, turn budget and permissions.",
    "Headline: an MCP server is only as good as the pointer to it. Attached alone, agents called it in 3 of 24 runs and reused DS components in 4 of 18 build runs, no better than the control (6 of 18). Add one line naming the server and agents called it in 22 of 24 runs (4.7 calls each on average) and reused DS components in 15 of 18, level with documenting the CLI (14 of 18). The client defers MCP tools behind a tool search, so an agent that is not told the server exists rarely looks.",
    "The pointer line, verbatim: \"This repository's design system is available through the `design-system` MCP server; use its tools to find components and validate usage before finishing.\" Cost of the pointer: about $0.10 more per run than the MCP arm, from the extra tool calls.",
    "Pass rates saturated. First-try pass is 23 or 24 of 24 in every arm. The three v2 tasks (phantom tokens, modal focus, form error wiring) did not separate the arms for this model, and no run in any arm referenced an undefined token. Reuse is reported and never gates a pass.",
    "Isolation: runs pass --strict-mcp-config and --setting-sources project,local, so the operator's user-level Claude configuration never reaches the agent. The August batch (archived) loaded it in both arms and is not pooled with these numbers.",
    "Grader fixes during the batch: the migration acceptance hardcoded a consumer file that no longer uses Badge, and the colour scan flagged the real token var(--color-white). Both were fixed, guarded in the selftest, and those tasks re-run in the first three arms; superseded runs are listed in supersededRuns and excluded. The MCP + POINTER arm ran the next day against the same source commit with the fixed graders. Total spend including superseded runs: $74.07 ($28.19 superseded).",
    "n=3 per arm per task, claude-sonnet-5, 30-turn budget, automatic repair loop. With n=3, treat per-task differences as anecdotes; the MCP call rate and the reuse gap are the differences large and consistent enough to read."
